<title>DENMARK: SAS slides ahead of Q1 results.</title>
<headline>SAS slides ahead of Q1 results.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS) shares fell by 2.85 percent on the Copenhagen Stock Exchange on Tuesday, ahead of first quarter results expected to show a sharp fall in profits.</p>
<p>At 1025 GMT the share was at 68 Danish crowns, down two crowns from Monday's close.</p>
<p>Analysts expect the results, to be published on Tuesday afternoon, to show a 45 percent drop in pre-tax profits compared to the first quarter of 1996. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
